anine Driscoll roughly 19-to-1, and most raters call the race Likely D or safer. Prediction markets at 91-95% for Democrats and the absence of any credible polling showing a competitive race justify only a modest trim from the baseline.", "watch": "The announced House Republican TV ad campaign against Gillen, if it proves large and effective, could narrow the margin in a district that is only modestly Democratic.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["No usable general-election polls; forecast rests on fundamentals and expert ratings.", "Incumbent Laura Gillen (D) is running."]}, "overview": "First-term incumbent Laura Gillen defends a Long Island seat with a modest Democratic lean of about two points. She enters the fall with a dominant financial position, having raised over $5 million and holding $3.8 million on hand, while Republican Jeanine Driscoll has raised roughly $265,000. A Libertarian candidate trails with minimal resources.\n\nNo public general-election polling is available, so the outlook rests on fundamentals, expert ratings, and markets. Most raters place the race at Likely D or better, though Inside Elections rates it Tilt D and Sabato's Crystal Ball rates it Lean D. Prediction markets price Gillen's chances around 91%. House Republicans have announced a television ad campaign targeting her, and Driscoll has attacked her tax votes, but the challenger faces a steep resource gap in a favorable Democratic year.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.9622, "margin": 11.83}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.9401, "margin": 10.5}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.9422, "margin": 10.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.9272, "margin": 10.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.9344, "margin": 11.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.9323, "margin": 11.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.9557, "margin": 11.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.9565, "margin": 11.5}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.9413, "margin": 10.5}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_